A||||3||DaveL||Clunking Rear End||||5||
Z||000000||DaveL||10-21-2000||08:41 AM||||My 87 SE 2.5 has suddenly started making this rather loud clunk when I put it into gear. Thought it was just the dogbone, but replaceing it made no difference. The noise seems to be coming from the right rear. Do you think this could be the motor mount? If so, how hard are they to replace? This is an automatic, and the Fiero store shows a motor mount but says the tranny mount is unavailable.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||10-21-2000||08:44 AM||||You most likely have a bad C/V joint, check your axels.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Xtreme Fiero's||10-21-2000||12:31 PM||||I have learned from OGRE that the DIS 4-bangers only have two motor mounts. I'd look there. <P>Open the deck lid and watch the motor while some one goes from D to N to R (slowly). I'd bet your motor is danci'n away in there and the Manifold is hiting the Trunk wall (thus your clunk) ||||reg||2
Z||000003||theogre||10-21-2000||05:52 PM||||The 87 4 cyl auto has one mount under the engine and one under a huge tranny bracket. Stick tranny has 2 mounts.<P>The one under the motor is likely shot, but still check the axles.<P>Also if you put in a new dogbone with rubber bushings you have to push the motor all the way on the automatic. The rubber bushing will still let the air cleaner hit the trunk wall.||||reg||1
